 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "c0_0",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#band\n# How it reads with text\nThe only question a backdrop has to answer: can this be read across a room,\nfor twenty minutes, without anyone squinting.\n---\n### Raise dim: if\n- The card edges disappear into the picture\n- A heading over the picture is hard to find\n- The picture keeps catching your eye mid-sentence\n---\n### Lower dim: if\n- The picture may as well be a flat colour\n- The deck feels heavier than what it is saying\n",
   "x": 80,
   "y": 80,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "c0_1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#stat\n# 0.5\n\nThe dim on this deck. One line on the `#deck` card, and the only number here worth arguing about.\n",
   "x": 1600,
   "y": 80,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "c0_2",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#section\n# Over a picture\nA divider is the one card that should stop the picture dead.\n",
   "x": 3120,
   "y": 80,
   "width": 1280,
   "height": 860
  },
  {
   "id": "g0",
   "type": "group",
   "label": "The look",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 4480,
   "height": 1020
  },
  {
   "id": "deck",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "#deck\n\ntheme: Atlas/Themes/Midnight.css\nimage: Atlas/Backdrops/Deep water.svg\ndim: 0.5\nheader: {deck}  ·  {n}/{total}\n\n# Deep water\n**Dark and quiet. Half the picture dimmed away, which is what a dense deck wants.**\n\n`Midnight.css` · `dim: 0.5`\n",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -1100,
   "width": 4480,
   "height": 860
  }
 ],
